cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or reference its experimental simulation results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Blockchain-Assisted Privacy-Preserving Federated Learning for Network Intrusion Detection with Trust-Based Security and Cryptographic Auditing"
abstract: >-
  A Python-based research simulation platform integrating federated learning (five
  simulated clients with Non-IID Dirichlet partitioning), client-level differential
  privacy (OS-CSPRNG Gaussian noise and Renyi Differential Privacy accounting),
  privacy-aware multi-criteria trust calibration against Byzantine poisoning, a
  locally simulated tamper-evident SHA-256 and ECDSA audit ledger, and an
  interactive Streamlit dashboard for network intrusion detection on NSL-KDD.
repository-code: "https://github.com/RanvyGHBs/blockchain-fl-ids"
